<content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>A squirrel runs up and down a tree.</para>
<para>The graph shows the height of the squirrel, \(h\) (feet), as a function of time, \(t\) (seconds).</para>
<media><image alt="Piecewise graph. Horizontal axis, 0 to 8, time, seconds. Vertical axis, 0 to 16, height, feet. Graph starts at 0 comma 9, increases, deceases to 4 comma 0, increases, then flattens out at 6 comma 10." src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/50aa7651b1fe19a899593f61b9abfcf0b087a126"/></media><!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>What is the highest point the squirrel reaches?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>14 feet</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Solve \(h(t)=0\). What does this solution tell you about the squirrel?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\(t=4\) means that after 4 seconds, the squirrel is at the bottom of the tree on the ground.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>Find the vertical intercept of the graph. What does it tell you about the squirrel?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>\((0,9)\) means that at the beginning, the squirrel is 9 feet high in the tree.
    </para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
